WEBVTT

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.970
"Discipline Committee Room"

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.970
Sup? Hirano, the teacher
told me to give you this.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.140
Thanks.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.930
Oh, hey, Mya-<i>chan</i>. Wanna head out with me?

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.520
Wait, you guys leave together?

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.230
We're on the same train line.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.400
Oh.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.730
I want to stop by the
bookstore, so not today.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.190
I'd better get going.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.530
Okay. See ya.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.530
Hey, Mya-<i>chan</i>, wait up!

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.410
Have fun.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.490
M-My visit to the bookstore today
is meant to be a solo trip.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.160
Are ya buyin' BL?

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.370
Don't just ask me that!

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.000
Yes, if you must know.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.460
Wouldn't it be easier together?

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.670
You try standing in front of
the BL shelf with another guy!

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.050
You'll just end up fodder
for everyone's conversations!

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.340
You sure about that?

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.010
Yes, I am.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:00.930
Then I'll stand at a different shelf.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.560
I guess that... would be fine...

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.810
"First time tagging along"

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.780
Look at all the books they've got here.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:20.120
"Miyano's first time here"

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.250
You aren't nervous?

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.290
Huh? It's just manga, right?

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:28.210
R-Right.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:30.090
Normies are so strong.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.880
"He Says Love Is Everything"

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:02.450
"Sasaki and Miyano"

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.440
"Episode 2: 'Someone I Like'"
Bread for lunch today?

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.700
"Episode 2: 'Someone I Like'"
Yup. It's flaming pollack roe and
mushroom salted bread. Autumn only.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.410
Mya-<i>chan</i>!

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:24.780
--It's that guy again.
--Senpai.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.450
Miyano, you've got a visitor.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.160
Thanks.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.200
Manga?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.040
Yeah.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.830
So he's seriously reading BL, too.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.250
Yeah.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.380
I finished it. Next volume please.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.470
Here.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.430
Thanks.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:52.810
What is it?

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.530
Senpai, I know you said
these manga were good, but...

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:01.860
Yeah.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:08.540
H-How can you want to read them
even without being a <i>fudanshi</i>?

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.160
Huh?

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.790
I just... don't get the appeal
without the <i>moe</i>...

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:16.250
...s-since I'm a <i>fudanshi</i>...

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:21.380
If there's someone I like,
I want to know them.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:25.590
"someone I like"

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.800
G-G-G-Go to your classroom!

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.560
The bell rings soon!

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.640
Oh, yeah. See ya later.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:43.950
What is he thinking?

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.910
Same with the "going out" thing.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:48.490
He's gonna be misinterpreted.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.460
Your face is beet red.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.040
You're imagining it.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.710
It sorta sounded like he said
"someone I like."

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:00.920
Senpai jokes like that a lot.

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:05.180
What?

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.470
Oh, nothing.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.160
Whatcha listening to?

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:35.000
You dummy, A-Are you crazy,
doing that <i>here</i>?

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.250
It's your own fault.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:37.460
S-Stop!

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.170
I-It's not what you think!
Really, it's not!

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:43.760
I just accidentally put it in
with my music!

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.720
I'm not walking around listening to this!

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:49.340
In fact, I barely listened
to any of it! I swear!

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.390
Are you crazy, doing that--

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:58.770
Oh, I can't take it!

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:02.070
Please just forget this ever happened!

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:05.740
What was that, anyway?

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:07.450
A drama CD.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.070
A drama CD?

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:14.870
There are CDs that contain stories
told purely through audio.

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:18.330
"Is it BL?"

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:18.330
"You dummy, A-Are you crazy,
doing that <i>here</i>?"

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:19.670
"You dummy, A-Are you crazy,
doing that <i>here</i>?"

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.130
"Yes. It's BL."
Senpai, please get
immediate amnesia. I'll help.

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:24.000
Senpai, please get
immediate amnesia. I'll help.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.340
Mya-<i>chan </i>is so cute.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.760
Oh, hey, Miyano.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:31.930
Whatcha doin'?

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:33.180
Having an <i>otaku </i>fit?

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:34.760
Leave me alone.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.890
Y'know how Miyano's face is feminine?

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.400
--When he blushes, could you
mistake him for a girl?

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.110
--Senpai, you can't immediately
imitate BL like that. Seriously.
--When he blushes, could you
mistake him for a girl?

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.320
--Senpai, you can't immediately
imitate BL like that. Seriously.
--What? No way. He's a dude.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:47.530
--Senpai, you can't immediately
imitate BL like that. Seriously.
--Yeah, I wouldn't either.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:52.120
Senpai, are you listening?

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:54.410
Senpai?

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:59.290
What are you doing?

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.330
Huh?

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:03.170
No, really.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:05.250
Miyano.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.420
Sorry I took so long.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:07.840
Hi, Senpai.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:09.090
Hey.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.180
I had an awful time waiting for you.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:13.800
Nature called. Forgive me.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:17.140
Did something happen?

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:19.680
Oh, Senpai, don't you have class?

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.850
Yeah, I gotta go.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.100
See ya.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.730
What were you two doing?

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:28.400
That's what I'd like to know.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.290
What was that all about?

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.750
Mya-<i>chan</i>, let's play a game!

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.130
No. I'm filling out my journal sheet.

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.840
Huh? How come?

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:55.510
Games of chicken are really popular
in my class right now.

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.220
Chicken?

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:01.810
The one where your faces get closer
and closer until someone bails.

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:03.940
Oh, a normie game.

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:05.230
Huh?

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:10.650
So what put this idea in your head?

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.780
I just wanted to try it
with you, Mya-<i>chan</i>.

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:17.370
--And maybe it ends with a lucky--
--There you go repeating BL nonsense.

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:18.490
Party pooper.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:22.750
Well, would you like some of these,
Mya-<i>chan</i>? They're not sweet.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:27.130
Maybe he really did buy these
for this purpose...

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:29.630
Well, if they're not particularly sweet...

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:49.230
"Thu., Nov. 11th" "Weather: Sunny"
"Name: Miyano"

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:02.750
Um, it feels pretty awkward to go
all the way to your hand.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:05.290
Could you let go?

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:07.540
Yeah, sure.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.880
Oh, you can have the rest of them.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:10.750
See ya.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.510
Oh, okay. Bye.

00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:31.900
It's sweet.

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:55.760
Does he have no guard up? Is it gone?

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:02.850
He usually gets mad.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:11.770
I don't know anymore!

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:15.280
Damn. He's so cute.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:17.650
It's gotten pretty bad.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.820
I feel like...

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:23.540
...next time I hug him,
I'm liable to squeeze extra hard.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.790
And then Mya-<i>chan </i>will...

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:32.340
...be upset, huh?

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:41.800
I'll have to be careful not to touch him.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.310
Miyano, I got the key.

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:53.650
Let's turn in the journal and go home.

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:55.230
Yeah...

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.530
Where'd those come from?

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:59.700
Sasaki-<i>senpai </i>just gave them to me.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.490
Really? You gonna eat 'em?

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:03.620
Do you like those?

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:05.740
Since they were a gift, I'll eat them.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:08.040
It's not like they're intolerable.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:11.750
The other day when I gave you
chocolates, you gave them away.

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:13.840
Those were sweet.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:15.340
I sense a difference in treatment.

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:16.800
There isn't one.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.420
Okay sure.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:21.050
Whatever. I'll just buy some
for my girlfriend.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:26.100
There isn't...

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:27.390
...is there?

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:34.690
"Mon., Nov. 15th"

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:34.690
Kuresawa, you still here?

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.440
"Mon., Nov. 15th"

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.440
You barely caught me.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:39.940
I'm really sorry!
Please turn in my notebook!

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:40.780
Not forgiven.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.160
Forgive me!

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:44.280
Oh, Miyano, you're still here, too.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:49.200
Yeah, I'm finishing the journal.
I'm on duty this week, too.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.830
Oh, yeah, I've been meaning
to ask ya somethin'.

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:54.290
Are you and that <i>senpai </i>who visits so much

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:56.040
going out?

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.210
What kind of question is that?!

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:02.590
Well, this <i>is </i>an all-boys school,
and he calls you cute all the time.

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:03.470
W-We're not.

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:05.430
Then he's taking advantage?

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:06.510
No!

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:08.890
We have a normal
<i>senpai</i>-<i>kouhai </i>relationship!

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:11.770
You call your manga arrangement normal?

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:13.900
Shut it, Kuresawa.

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:19.530
Well, if you're fine, then it's all good.

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:24.820
You expressed concern before, too.
Is Sasaki-<i>senpai </i>scary?

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:28.450
Isn't anybody who's older and bigger?

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:32.080
Well, you do have a point...

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:34.170
Sasaki-<i>senpai </i>is a good person.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:36.500
Huh?

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:39.210
Remember when I got beat up
before summer break?

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:42.630
It was Sasaki-<i>senpai </i>that saved me.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:49.930
What do <i>you </i>want?

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:52.180
I'm cleaning up here.

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:55.150
You okay? You should get going.

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:56.860
Y-Yes.

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:00.610
Huh.

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:04.650
So it's just that he has an
exceptional relationship with Miyano.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:05.660
Exactly.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:07.950
Not "exactly" at all!

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:10.160
Well, I got club stuff to get back to.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:11.910
I'll go turn in these notebooks.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:13.000
Okay.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.540
See ya!

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:23.130
Did only one person leave early today?

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:27.550
"Left Early | Absent"

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:31.220
I'm sure they were only joking about it,

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:35.640
but I wonder if Senpai is also
being teased in class in some way...

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:43.110
Is he being looked at in that way
because I'm lending him BL manga?

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.030
If he is, what do I d--

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:46.910
Mya-<i>chan</i>!

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:49.990
What? Senpai? What brings you here?

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:51.870
My bad.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:54.200
I dropped by because
I heard you were still here.

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:59.380
Mya-<i>chan</i>, do you get hit on a lot?

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:01.290
What brought that up all of a sudden?

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:06.420
Is relationship gossip the new trend
among high school boys?

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:10.430
Actually, you should abandon this notion
that there are potential partners

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:11.720
behind every corner.

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:14.180
They're not that plentiful.

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:16.020
What about Hirano?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.850
Hirano-<i>senpai </i>is an <i>uke</i>.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:19.980
<i>He's </i>an <i>uke</i>?

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:22.610
Got it. Continue.

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:25.360
He's with the younger student
who is his roommate.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:27.950
Bold move, <i>fudanshi</i>.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:31.370
But put all that aside for the moment.

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:37.250
Though this is a boys' school, there's
a coed school nearby, and we can work,

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:41.420
so it's actually more common for
students to find a girlfriend off-campus.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:44.670
I thought you chose this school
because it was a boys' school.

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:47.840
What kind of conception
of <i>fudanshi </i>do you have?

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:50.840
They'll do anything
to achieve their goals.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:52.390
According to one of the manga I borrowed.

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:53.430
Manga?!

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:56.270
Miyano, you idiot!

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:58.980
Anyway, that's not why I came here.

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:03.610
Besides, I found BL
after I chose this school.

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:05.780
And it was unintentional.

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:08.280
Unintentional?

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:13.580
Then how did you start
reading BL, Mya-<i>chan</i>?

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:16.830
People... are fallible
and prone to error...

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:20.920
Uh-huh.

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:38.020
A r-reference book...

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.480
Yeah.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:45.270
I went to get a reference book
for exams and manga for study breaks,

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:51.110
when I spotted a manga with a familiar
character drawn really well on the cover.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:54.030
It said "anthology" on it,

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:58.160
and there are sometimes official
collaborations between authors,

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:01.120
so I thought it was something like that.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.310
Um...

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:26.900
Uh-huh, and that turned out to be BL.

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:29.650
It was partly my fault for being careless,

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:31.530
but it was hard to figure out!

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.860
It was on a normal shelf!

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:35.450
I see.

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:40.330
And I bet he later went out and
found several similar titles to buy.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:41.910
He's so cute.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.250
Are you listening?

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:51.090
Yep.

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:55.340
I just remembered. I saw an ad in a
convenience store for BL-looking manga.

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:56.680
Mya-<i>chan</i>, do you know about it?

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:58.890
Can you tell me the title?

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:00.770
Uh, let's see now...

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:28.170
Hirano, you still here?

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:29.000
What is it?

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.550
Oh, Sasaki-<i>senpai</i>.

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:32.050
Oh, it's Mya-<i>chan</i>!

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:33.760
Heading home now?

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:34.840
Yes.

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:37.510
Did you need to see me
or not? I'm leaving.

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:41.060
Hold on, now. There it is.
From our teacher.

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:42.310
Thanks.

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:45.980
Actually, you've been on
gopher duty a lot lately.

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.400
More post-graduation stuff?

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:53.900
Yeah. When you're a second year, you'll
also be told to squeeze in school visits.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:56.110
Keep your head up.

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:58.110
But I've barely even
started at this school.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:00.080
"February"

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:02.120
"February"

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:02.120
It's been almost a year though.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.120
"February"

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.120
Time really flew.

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:05.250
Time really flew.

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:09.210
I'll go hand in the key,
so you can head home, Miyano.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:10.960
You're leaving now, too, right?

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:12.090
Yup.

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:14.300
Then I'll head out now.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:15.300
Bye.

